    "question": {
      ":question/id": "107b0d08-c0c2-5e3b-a247-c4238dbd6d8f",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{8} & \\frac{9}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{9} & -\\frac{9}{7}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{8} & \\frac{9}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{9} & -\\frac{9}{7}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot (-\\frac{9}{7})-\\frac{9}{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{9}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{45}{56}-(-\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{113}{280}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
